Tavletta for Debian
===================

Printers on USB
---------------

The package installs a udev rule (/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-tavletta.rules)
that lets the user at the computer, in an active local session, use USB
printers on the kernel's printer class driver (/dev/usb/lp*) and NIIMBOT
printers (a USB serial port, /dev/ttyACM*, vendor 3513). It takes effect
when the printer is plugged in again. Users who print from elsewhere (an SSH
session, a service) need the group lp, for NIIMBOT printers dialout:

  sudo usermod -aG lp,dialout USER

The print server
----------------

tavletta-server.service runs `tavletta serve` as the system user tavletta
(made by the package), sandboxed, on 127.0.0.1:8790. It is installed but
neither enabled nor started. Its files:

  /etc/tavletta/printers.toml   the printers clients may use
  /etc/tavletta/tokens.toml     the access tokens (hashes)
  /var/lib/tavletta/labels/     the label files

Both TOML files belong to tavletta, mode 600. Make a token as that user:

  sudo -u tavletta tavletta token new NAME --role print \
      --tokens /etc/tavletta/tokens.toml --printers /etc/tavletta/printers.toml
  sudo systemctl enable --now tavletta-server

The service has no access to devices: it prints to network printers. The
full guide, with a reverse proxy for HTTPS:
https://tavletta.joshuahirsig.xyz/server-install/
